        "content": "I have gathered all the essential information. Let me compile the comprehensive report.\n\n## Resource Download System Analysis — Complete Findings\n\n### Overview\n\nThe download system lives almost entirely in `Assets/MJAssetsFrame/Runtime/BundleHot/` (namespace `MJ.AssetFrameWork.ABFrame`). **Note:** The term \"负载均衡/LoadBalance\" does **not** exist literally in the codebase — the concept is implemented as **thread-count balancing** (`MultipleThreadBalancing()`, `SetDownLoadThreadCount`). There is also **no enum named `E_DownloadState`/`DownloadState`** — download state is tracked via `bool` flags (`mIsFinished`), dictionaries/lists, and a wait queue, not an enum/state machine. Several files contain GBK-encoded Chinese comments that render as mojibake in UTF-8, but the code logic is intact.\n\n---\n\n### 1. HotAssetsModule — `Assets/MJAssetsFrame/Runtime/BundleHot/HotAssetsModule.cs`\n\nPer-module hot-update coordinator. Constructor takes a `BundleModuleEnum`.\n\n**State / progress tracking fields:**\n- `public BundleModuleEnum CurBundleModuleEnum { get; set; }` — current module\n- `public List<HotFileInfo> mNeedDownLoadAssetList` — files that actually need downloading\n- `public List<HotFileInfo> mAllHotAssetList` — all hot-update files in the server patch\n- `private HotAssetsManifest mServerHotAssetsManifest` / `mLocalHotAssetsManifest` — server/local manifests\n- `public int HotAssetCount => mAllHotAssetList.Count`\n- `public float mAssetsMaxSizeM { get; set; }` — total required download size (MB)\n- `public float mAssetDownLoadSizeM` — **accumulated downloaded bytes (updated by DownLoadThread)** — the progress counter\n- `private AssetDownLoader mAssetDownLoader`\n- `public Action<BundleModuleEnum> OnDownLoadAllAssetsFinish` — module-complete event\n\n**Key methods:**\n- `StartHotAssets(bool isCheckAssetsVersion = true)` — creates a `UniTaskCompletionSource`, subscribes to `OnDownLoadAllAssetsFinish`, optionally checks version, calls `StartDownLoadHotAssets()`, then `await tcs.Task` until all downloads finish.\n- `StartDownLoadHotAssets()` — builds `downLoadList` (files whose `abName` contains `\"bundleconfig\"` are **inserted at index 0** so the config bundle downloads first), enqueues into a `Queue<HotFileInfo> downLoadQueue`, then `new AssetDownLoader(this, downLoadQueue, mServerHotAssetsManifest.downLoadUrl, HotAssetsSavePath)` and calls `StartThreadDownLoadQueue()`.\n- `CheckAssetsVersion()` / `DownLoadHotAssetsManifest()` — manifest download with up to `MAX_MANIFEST_DOWN_LOAD_COUNT = 3` retries (30 s UnityWebRequest timeout, 1 s delay between retries); writes server manifest to `persistentDataPath/Server<Module>AssetsHotManifest.json`.\n- `ComputeNeedHotAssetsList(HotAssetsPatch)` — compares `HotAssetsSavePath + abName` file existence + MD5 (`MD5.GetMd5FromFile`) against server manifest; fills `mAllHotAssetList` / `mNeedDownLoadAssetList` and sums `mAssetsMaxSizeM += item.size / 1024f`.\n- `CheckModuleAssetsIsHot()` — compares local/server patch versions.\n- `SetDownLoadThreadCount(int threadCount)` — the load-balancing hook: sets `mAssetDownLoader.MAX_THREAD_COUNT` (logs `\"设置线程负载均衡:\"`).\n- **Callback region (bottom):**\n  - `DownLoadAssetBundleSuccess(HotFileInfo)` → strips `BundlePostfix`, and invokes **`HotAssetsManager.DownLoadBundleFinish?.Invoke(hotFileInfo)`** (special-cases `\"bundleconfig\"` files)\n  - `DownLoadAssetBundleFailed(HotFileInfo)` — empty stub\n  - `DownLoadAssetBundleFinish()` — deletes local manifest, copies server manifest → local path (`Local<Module>AssetsHotManifest.json`), invokes `OnDownLoadAllAssetsFinish?.Invoke(CurBundleModuleEnum)` then nulls the delegate.\n- `HotAssetsIsExists(string bundleName)`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. HotAssetsManager — orchestration + 负载均衡 (thread load balancing)\n\n`Assets/MJAssetsFrame/Runtime/BundleHot/HotAssetsManager.cs` (implements `IHotAssets`).\n\n**Fields:**\n- `private int MAX_THREAD_COUNT = 3;`\n- `Dictionary<BundleModuleEnum, HotAssetsModule> allAssetsModuleDic` — cached per-module instances\n- `Dictionary<BundleModuleEnum, HotAssetsModule> downLoadingAssetsModuleDic` — currently downloading\n- `List<HotAssetsModule> downLoadAssetsModuleList`\n- `Queue<WaitDownLoadModule> waitDownLoadModuleQueue` — **module-level wait queue** (`WaitDownLoadModule` holds `bundleModule` + `UniTaskCompletionSource tcs`)\n- `public static Action<HotFileInfo> DownLoadBundleFinish;` — **the per-file completion callback**\n\n**Multi-module scheduling (`HotAssets(BundleModuleEnum, bool)`):**\n- If `downLoadingAssetsModuleDic.Count < MAX_THREAD_COUNT` → start immediately (add to dict + list, call `MultipleThreadBalancing()`, `await assetsModule.StartHotAssets(...)`, then `HotModuleAssetsFinish(bundleModule)`).\n- Else → enqueue a `WaitDownLoadModule` with a TCS and **await it**; when released, add to downloads, balance, start.\n- **`HotModuleAssetsFinish(bundleModule)`** — removes module from `downLoadingAssetsModuleDic`/`downLoadAssetsModuleList`; if `waitDownLoadModuleQueue.Count > 0` dequeue and `tcs.TrySetResult()` (wakes the next awaiting module), else calls `MultipleThreadBalancing()`.\n\n**`MultipleThreadBalancing()` — the 负载均衡 logic:**\n```\ncount = downLoadingAssetsModuleDic.Count\nthreadCount = MAX_THREAD_COUNT * 1.0f / count   // e.g. 3/1=3, 3/2=1.5, 3/3=1\nint mainThreadCount = 0\nthreadBalancingCount = (int)threadCount\nif ((int)threadCount < threadCount) {  // fractional\n    mainThreadCount = CeilToInt(threadCount)\n    threadBalancingCount = FloorToInt(threadCount)\n}\n// first module in iteration gets mainThreadCount, rest get threadBalancingCount\n```\nSo with 3 max threads: 1 module→3 threads; 2 modules→2+1; 3 modules→1+1+1. Each module then receives `SetDownLoadThreadCount(...)`.\n\nAlso: `GetOrNewAssetModule`, `CheckAssetsVersion(module)`, `GetHotAssetsModule(module)`, and a stub `OnMainThreadUpdate()`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. AssetDownLoader — the download queue engine\n\n**`Assets/MJAssetsFrame/Runtime/BundleHot/AssetDownLoader.cs`**\n\n- `public int MAX_THREAD_COUNT = 3;`\n- `private Queue<HotFileInfo> downLoadQueue` — **download queue**\n- `private List<DownLoadThread> mAllDownLoadThreadList` — active download threads\n- `private bool mIsFinished` — **guards against duplicate finish callbacks**\n- `StartThreadDownLoadQueue()` — `lock(mAllDownLoadThreadList)`, spawns up to `MAX_THREAD_COUNT` parallel `StartDownLoadNextBundle().Forget()` calls while `downLoadQueue.Count > 0`.\n- `DownLoadNextBundle()` — lock the list: if queue non-empty → start next; else if **queue empty AND no active threads** → `mIsFinished = true; curHotAssetsModule.DownLoadAssetBundleFinish();`\n- `RemoveDownLoadThread(thread)` — removes a finished thread from the active list.\n- `StartDownLoadNextBundle()` — dequeue `HotFileInfo`, create `new AssetDownLoader`... actually `new DownLoadThread(curHotAssetsModule, hotFileInfo, url, savePath)`, add to active list, `await downLoadItem.StartDownLoad()`, remove thread, then route to `DownLoadAssetBundleSuccess` / `DownLoadAssetBundleFailed`, then recursively `DownLoadNextBundle()`.\n\n**No state enum exists here — the state machine is: queue → active-thread list → finish flag.**\n\n---\n\n### 4. Download state tracking — DownLoadThread\n\n**Path: `Assets/MJAssetsFrame/Runtime/BundleHot/DownLoadThread.cs`**\n\n- `private const int Max_TRY_DOWNLOAD_COUNT = 3;` — per-file retry\n- `StartDownLoad()` — a `for` retry loop; downloads via raw `HttpWebRequest` on `UniTask.RunOnThreadPool`, reads 512-byte buffer, writes to `mFileSavePath` (`savePath + \"/\" + abName`), accumulates `downLoadedSize`; on success: **`mCurAssetsHotModule.mAssetDownLoadSizeM += downloadedSize/1024f/1024f`** (this is where progress is updated); returns `bool success`. Returns `false` after 3 failed attempts.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Manifest data — `HotAssetsManifest.cs`\n\n- `HotAssetsManifest` { `updateNotice`, `downLoadUrl`, `List<HotAssetsPatch> hotAssetsPatcheList` }\n- `HotAssetsPatch` { `int patchVersion`, `List<HotFileInfo> hotAssetsList` }\n- `HotFileInfo` { `abName`, `md5`, `size` }\n\n---\n\n### 6. How `DownLoadBundleFinish` works (callback chain)\n\n1. Declared as **static** in `HotAssetsManager`: `public static Action<HotFileInfo> DownLoadBundleFinish;`\n2. Subscribed in `ResourcesManager.Initlizate()` (in `Assets/MJAssetsFrame/Runtime/BundleLoad/ResourcesManager.cs` line 72): `HotAssetsManager.DownLoadBundleFinish += AssetsDownLoadFinish;`\n3. Raised per-file by `HotAssetsModule.DownLoadAssetBundleSuccess()` after each file's download thread completes.\n4. **`AssetsDownLoadFinish(HotFileInfo info)`** (ResourcesManager.cs ~L79–L135):\n   - Files with `\"bundleconfig\"` in `abName` → re-processes the whole `mWaitLoadAndCloneAssetsList` (config arrives first, so pending downloads can then resolve).\n   - If `mWaitDownloadTcs.Count > 0` → looks up `AssetBundleManager.Instance.GetBundleItemByAbName(info.abName)`; if the bundle config isn't loaded yet (`Count == 0`, race protection since multi-thread download can exceed asset loading), it **buffers the item in `mWaitLoadAndCloneAssetsList`** and returns; otherwise it computes `crc = Crc32.GetCrc32(path)` per `BundleItem` and `mWaitDownloadTcs[crc].TrySetResult()` — waking any loader awaiting that asset (see L380–L389 where the TCS is created on demand and L616–L619 where it's canceled on cleanup).\n\nSo `DownLoadBundleFinish` is a **per-file bridge between the hot-download pipeline and the on-demand load pipeline**, letting `ResourcesManager` instantiate/preload a hot-updated bundle the moment its file lands, with a wait-list fallback when the bundle manifest isn't parsed yet.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Supporting/entry files\n\n- **`Assets/MJAssetsFrame/MJAssetsABFrames.cs`** — static facade: `HotAssets(module, isCheckVersion)` → `instance.mHotAssets.HotAssets(...)`, `CheckAssetsVersion`, `GetHotAssetsModule`, `StartDeCompressBuiltinFile`, `WaitDeCompress`.\n- **`HotUpdateManager.cs`** — high-level flow